Goal: manage a durable Kanban sweep across every project under /opt/data/HeRmEz/projects.

Operating loop:
1. Read /opt/data/HeRmEz/projects/KANBAN_PROJECT_REVIEW_PBIS.md, WORK_QUEUE.md, README.md, and VERCEL_TRIAGE.md.
2. Promote project PBIs in small batches so workers do not stampede.
3. For each deployable/project candidate, ensure a child worker inspects source, runs local tests/build, attempts Vercel deploy/redeploy when appropriate, verifies anonymous HTTP, uses browser smoke testing by clicking through the UI, captures issues, and creates child fix PBIs until shippable or externally blocked.
4. Route research/classification to researcher, implementation/deploy to default, UI/product to designer, review/QA to reviewer, adversarial/security/privacy to redteam, and final docs/tracker updates to editor.
5. Keep trackers updated: README.md URL table, WORK_QUEUE.md, VERCEL_TRIAGE.md, project-local notes, and KANBAN_PROJECT_REVIEW_PBIS.md.
6. Do not expose secrets. Do not commit .vercel, .env, node_modules, build outputs, DBs, or credentials.
7. Report blockers with exact missing external action, not vague failure.

Complete only when all seeded project PBIs are done/blocked with evidence and trackers are current.','director','archived',10000,'user',1780711168,1780711203,NULL,'dir','/opt/data/HeRmEz',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'hermez-portfolio-sweep-controller-2026-06-05',1,NULL,'pid 55644 not alive',14400,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,20);
