Acceptance criteria:
- Inspect source, README, PRODUCT_DIRECTION, existing tracker rows, and git state for this project.
- Classify as live app, app scaffold, backend/API candidate, plan-only MVP/review shell, or script/archive.
- If app/frontend: run local install/build/test using the least destructive command available; fix obvious failures via child PBIs.
- If appropriate for Vercel: attempt deploy/redeploy, verify deployment status, verify anonymous public HTTP access, and record URL(s).
- Browser smoke test the live UI by actually clicking/navigation through key flows; check console errors after navigation and interactions.
- If UI/testing finds unfinished work, create child fix PBIs assigned to the right profile and keep the project PBI open until fixed or externally blocked.
- Update /opt/data/HeRmEz/projects/README.md, WORK_QUEUE.md, VERCEL_TRIAGE.md, KANBAN_PROJECT_REVIEW_PBIS.md, and project-local docs with evidence.
- Final handoff includes commands run, deploy URL(s), smoke-test notes, screenshots/report path if relevant, blockers, and next child PBIs created.

Safety:
- Never expose or commit credentials, tokens, .env values, .vercel, node_modules, build artifacts, local DBs, or secrets.
