URL: https://faceless-youtube-channel-beta.vercel.app/#costs
Report: /opt/data/kanban/workspaces/t_a9718870/dogfood-output/report.md

Severity: Low
Category: Functional / UX

Steps to reproduce:
1. Open a new browser navigation directly to `https://faceless-youtube-channel-beta.vercel.app/#costs`.
2. Wait for the React app to finish loading.
3. Observe the viewport and scroll position.

Expected behavior:
- The page should scroll to the `Cheap/free by default` / costs section matching the `#costs` anchor.

Actual behavior:
- URL contains `#costs`, but the viewport remains at the top of the page.
- Observed browser state: `window.scrollY` was 0 while `document.querySelector(''#costs'').getBoundingClientRect().top` was approximately 2168px.
- DOM-triggered click of `a[href="#costs"]` after render did scroll correctly, so the issue appears limited to direct hash loads before the React-rendered anchor exists.

Suggested fix:
- On app mount, if `window.location.hash` exists, find the matching element after render and call `scrollIntoView()`. A `useEffect` plus `requestAnimationFrame`/post-render callback is likely sufficient.

Acceptance criteria:
- Direct loads to `/#pipeline` and `/#costs` land at the intended sections.
- Existing in-page CTA clicks still work.
- No console errors on direct hash load or CTA clicks.','web-worker','ready',0,'default',1780730524,NULL,NULL,'scratch',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'20260606_070914_c3af6c',0,NULL);
